<Base {...head}>
<section class="books-index">
  <a class="back-link" href="/about/">&larr; About the Author</a>
  <div class="kicker">About · The Maker</div>
  <h2>Ink <span class="amp">&amp;</span> Iron <em>Apps</em>.</h2>
  <p class="lede">Small, sharp tools for makers, readers, and small operations — the software half of <a href="/about/">Riley E. Antrobus</a>'s workshop.</p>
  <div class="essay">
    <p>Ink &amp; Iron Apps is the software side of one workshop. Same hands that write the books build the apps: stories that take their time, and tools that don't waste yours.</p>
    <p class="pull">"Crafted stories. Forged software."</p>
    <p>The philosophy is narrow on purpose — each app does one job well for the people who actually need it, rather than a sprawling suite that does everything adequately. Some run on the web so they work everywhere; others are Android first. No ads, no dark patterns, no selling your data.</p>
    <p><a href="/apps/libraryiq.html">LibraryIQ</a> is <strong>live</strong> — a reading tracker you can open right now at <a href="https://libraryiq.inknironapps.com" rel="noopener">libraryiq.inknironapps.com</a>, free, with nothing to install. MatCalc and Simmer are still in <strong>closed alpha testing</strong> on Android — no Play Store release yet. Want to help shape one? <a href="/contact.html?topic=general">Pick an app on the contact form</a> to join alpha testing.</p>
  </div>

